  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">A.1. The Government of Romania has reported on progress achieved under the international Sendai Framework for Disaster Risk Reduction.</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2018-05-25" value="0.00" year="2018"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2018-05-25"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="1.00">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&amp;gt;Four reports (2018, 2019, 2020, 2021) were submitted by DES and GIES on the Sendai Monitor platform&amp;nbsp;to monitor the progress achieved under the Sendai Framework for Disaster Risk Reduction.&lt;/p&amp;gt;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="4.00"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">A.3. Reports are available annually on the impact of disasters in Romania.</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2018-05-25" value="0.00" year="2018"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2018-05-25"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="3.00">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&amp;gt;Four reports were made public for years 2018, 2019, 2020, and 2021 on the impact of disasters in Romania&lt;strong&amp;gt;.&lt;/strong&amp;gt;&lt;/p&amp;gt;

&lt;p&amp;gt;Two types of reports were published annually on the IGSU website. These were respectively reports with an analysis of emergency response operations (&amp;ldquo;Analiza operative&amp;rdquo;) and data and information on the impact of hydro-meteorological events (&amp;ldquo;Valoarea pagubelor produse de evenimente hidro-meteorologice periculoase&amp;rdquo;). These were based on underlying SMISU data&amp;nbsp;and loss and damage data collected by DES and GIES.&lt;/p&amp;gt;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="4.00"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">A.2. Romanian citizens have enhanced understanding of the potential impacts of disasters and how they can prevent, prepare and respond to disasters through public awareness campaigns, drills and digit</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2018-05-25" value="0.00" year="2018"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2018-05-25"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="6.00">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&amp;gt;Six&lt;strong&amp;gt; &lt;/strong&amp;gt;dedicated and comprehensive government programs with an awareness campaign program (including 32 single campaigns), drill program (including 4,675 individual drills), apps and digital media tools (including one app, 2 digital platforms) were developed, implemented and became fully operational.&lt;/p&amp;gt;

&lt;p&amp;gt;The original target was a simple target focusing on the number of risk awareness campaigns. The indicator now is encompassing the number of government programs but that are comprised of more than 4,700 individual activities (risk awareness campaigns, drills, apps and platforms etc.).???????&lt;/p&amp;gt;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="6.00"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">B2. Disaster risk reduction action plans are prepared and approved by the relevant responsible authorities.</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2018-05-25" value="0.00" year="2018"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2018-05-25"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="3.00">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&amp;gt;Seven action plans/concepts were finalized and approved, namely i) concepts on epidemic situation in 2022, ii) concept on overall emergency response in 2022, iii) the second post-earthquake Response Concept in 2021, iv) the National Nuclear and/or RadiologicalAccident Response Concept in 2020; v) Regulation on the management of emergencies generated by dangerous meteorological phenomena resulting in the occurrence of pedological droughts in 2020, vi) Regulation on the management of emergencies generated by dangerous hydrometeorological phenomena in 2019, and vii) the national Response Concept for forest fires in 2018.&lt;/p&amp;gt;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="7.00"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
